  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CEMAC Trade and Transport Facilitation Strengthening</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the Grant is to assist CEMAC and its member states to:  - Monitor the implementation of trade and transport laws, - increase cooperation to facilitate corridor efficiency to Chad and CAR; - to improve the existing customs union, with a special emphasis on transit procedures to/from land locked countries The objectives of the grant are to assist CEMAC in reaching its main long term objective to create a common market for goods, services, capital and persons by:  - Strengthening the capacity of the CEMAC Secretariat and its member states to monitor implementation of trade  and transport laws and regulations and to develop a framework to enable members states to work together on corridor operations efficiency, using two pilot corridors between Cameroon and the two land-locked countries (CAR and Chad); and  - Developing an action plan to improve performance of the existing customs union with a special emphasis on transit procedures to and from land-locked countries.</narrative>
  </description>
